      "id": "ja-a1-04.l2",
      "title": "Beautiful, quiet, and things you like",
      "canDo": "I can describe places with な-adjectives and say what I like.",
      "intro": {
        "place": "lounge",
        "scene": "Sato shows Leo her photos of Kyoto.",
        "lines": [
          {
            "who": "佐藤",
            "text": "{京都|きょうと}{は|wa}きれいな{町|まち}ですよ。",
            "meaning": "Kyoto is a beautiful town, you know.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "レオ",
            "text": "{有名|ゆうめい}ですね。{静|しず}かですか。",
            "meaning": "It's famous, isn't it? Is it quiet?",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "佐藤",
            "text": "いいえ、あまり{静|しず}かじゃありません。とてもにぎやかです。",
            "meaning": "No, it's not very quiet. It's very lively.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "レオ",
            "text": "{佐藤|さとう}さん{は|wa}{京都|きょうと}が{好|す}きですか。",
            "meaning": "Do you like Kyoto?",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "佐藤",
            "text": "はい、{大好|だいす}きです。お{寺|てら}が{好|す}きです。",
            "meaning": "Yes, I love it. I like the temples.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "レオ",
            "text": "わたしも{古|ふる}い{町|まち}が{好|す}きです。",
            "meaning": "I like old towns too.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "title": "な-adjectives",
            "body": "The second family: きれい, {静|しず}か, にぎやか, {有名|ゆうめい}, {便利|べんり}. With です they behave like nouns: {静|しず}かです, {静|しず}かじゃありません. Before a noun they need な: きれいな{町|まち}, {有名|ゆうめい}なお{寺|てら}."
          },
          {
            "title": "Careful: きれい and {有名|ゆうめい}",
            "body": "They end in an \"i\" sound but are な-adjectives: きれいじゃありません, never きれくないです. Real い-adjectives go straight before a noun: {古|ふる}い{町|まち}, {新|あたら}しいホテル."
          },
          {
            "title": "〜が{好|す}きです",
            "body": "{好|す}き is a な-adjective meaning \"liked\", so the thing you like takes が: {猫|ねこ}が{好|す}きです. Stronger: {大好|だいす}きです. Not so much: あまり{好|す}きじゃありません."
          }
        ]
      },
